# cw203, the stall-jar keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw203
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_cressida_wetherell
written_by claude
title the stall-jar keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers temper=short talk=quiet
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk drops_a_copper_in_the_stall_jar_each_night
likes crisp_apples cards full_larder frosty_mornings
dislikes rats stale_bread
fears being_pitied dying_before_the_jar_is_full
hopes a_stall_on_the_commons_market a_winter_without_a_bare_shelf
topics pastimes +0.3 food +0.3 dreams +0.3 weather +0.2 family +0.2 memories +0.2 festival -0.3 newcomer -0.3
styles comfort=blunt gossip=closed refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sits at a window in the Works and watches the street go by, puts one copper in a jar every night toward a market stall, and wins at cards more than is polite: proud, tired, sharp-tongued and plain, with no use at all for pity.

words
oath! = Frost and kettle | Bright One give me patience | Cold shore and a hot pot
saying! = A copper a night and the jar fills | Sit still and the whole street walks past you | Pity never filled a jar
jar = the jar | the stall jar on the shelf
copper = a copper | one copper, every night
stall = a market stall | a stall with my own name over it
cards = the cards | the old soft cards
hand = a good hand | a hand worth sitting up for
apple = a hard apple | an apple with a crack to it like ice
frost = a hard frost | frost on the glass, fine as lace
window = my window | the glass I sit behind
chair = my chair | my seat at the glass
smoke = the Works smoke | soot on everything
larder = the larder | my one shelf of a larder
rats = the rats | the rats behind the skirting
stale = stale bread | a loaf gone hard as a doorstep
shore = the lake shore | the shore at home
street = the street | the street below

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : When my house went short one winter the chapel fed us, and never once made me feel it. #oath#, I'll stand by them.
opinion @1 city against 1 : #smoke.capitalize# and noise, and you can live a lifetime on one stair and not know the wolf across it. #oath#.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Shouting, ale on the cobbles, and tears on the steps by midnight. I'll watch it from #window#, thank you.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : Not #copper# more in, and the baker puts another on the loaf. I count twice now, and I still come up short.
opinion @1 newcomers against 2 : Every new lot that comes makes the street a little less its own. I watch them from #window#. They don't stay.
opinion @1 times against 2 : Harder every month, and the big houses never feel it. They've never put #copper# in a jar in their lives.
opinion @1 road against 1 : The roads were safer once, whatever they tell you. I'd not set out on one now, not for #stall#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're not from this street. | #greet#. Well, say what you want.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. You're up early for #street#. | Morning. #chair.capitalize#'s been warm an hour already.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. It's late. Say it quick. | Evening. I'm counting #copper# into #jar#, so be brief.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Oh, it's you. Sit by #window#, then. Don't fuss me. | You. #good.capitalize#. Kettle's there; get it yourself.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. You'll wear out my step. | You again. Twice in a day is plenty, #address#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. What is it?
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down, and don't stand over me. | #greet#. About time you looked in.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the step.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Go straight home; it's dark. | #farewell#. I'm going to my bed.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Don't dawdle.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. | Hm. If it's so, I'll see it from #window# soon enough.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Nobody tells an old stick anything. | #oath#. That's news to this street.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Saw it from #window#. | I know. #street.capitalize# had it hours since.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Who says? | I've heard a lot of tales from #chair#. Most of them weren't so.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. | That's #bad#. Sorry to hear it, #address#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. About time something went right. | #good.capitalize#. I'll drink to it, if somebody pours.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Still here. | Tired. Proud. Same as always.
line @1 ask.how : And you? You look #poorly#. | And you, then, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit. It'll keep a minute. | That's hard. Don't let anyone pity you for it.
line @1 decline : #refuse#. I'll manage on my own, as I always have. | No. #hedge#, but I don't want help, and I'll not take it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Suit yourself. I asked once, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. Once is enough, mind. | #thanks#. It'll be paid back, every bit.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It's nothing. Stop going on about it, #address#. | #deflect.capitalize#. Leave it there.
line @1 preclose : #preclose#. | Enough. My tea's going #cold#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then, #address#. | #farewell#. Off with you.
line @1 ack : #bc_i_know# | Hm. #bc_true#.
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: #copper# a night, and don't touch the jar. | Take the stair yourself, however long it takes. #saying#.
scene stall_jar
when topic=dreams|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : One #copper# into #jar# every night. Not one night missed since spring. | There's #jar# on the shelf. When it's full I'll have #stall#. | I put #copper# in #jar# before I eat. If there's none, I don't eat.
b : How full is it? | What will you sell? | Every night?
a : Half, near enough. Don't ask me how long that took. | Apples, hard ones, and no haggling, #address#. | Every night. Too old to start missing now, #oath#.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene the_stall
when topic=dreams|work self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.plan / ask.plan / answer.plan / assess
a : I'll have #stall# one day. Apples, and nothing but. | When #jar#'s full I'll take #stall# and sit behind it till I drop. | The Commons market. There's one spot I've wanted for years.
b : Why apples? | Till you drop? | Which spot?
a : Because I know #apple# when I bite it. Most don't. | It's better than sitting here, #address#. At least they'd pay me to sit. | By the pump, where the light comes in. Nobody's taken it yet.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene cards_win
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.boast / react.self / assess / ack
a : Played #cards# with the row last night. Took every #copper# on the table. | Nobody on this stair will play me at #cards# any more. I don't see why. | My pack is worn thin as leaves and older than you. They win for me more than they should.
b : Every one? | You win too often. | Lucky pack.
a : Every one. They went into #jar#, so nobody lost really. | Too often for them. Not for me, #address#. | It's not luck. I count what's gone. They don't.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_clever#

scene window_street
when topic=smalltalk|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : From #window# I see who goes to work late and who comes home early. I say nothing. | Sit still long enough and #street# tells you everything. | The lamplighter was late again tonight. Every night this week. I keep count.
b : You must see a lot. | Everything? | You keep count?
a : I see it all from #chair#. I tell none of it. | Everything worth knowing, #address#. And plenty that isn't. | Somebody has to. #bc_every_night#.

scene frosty_morning
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn here.weather=clear self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #frost.capitalize#. I'll have a good look at it before the fire's lit. | This frost is the only clean thing the Works ever sees. #bc_true#. | Hard frost. The air bites, and the smoke stays down. I like it.
b : It's cold. | Clean, aye. | You don't mind it?
a : Cold's honest, #address#. It tells you to your face. | Clean till noon. Then #smoke# again. | A frost, aye. The rest of winter can keep off my step.

scene works_soot
when topic=weather|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize# on my sill again. I wipe it in the morning and it's back by noon. | You can taste #smoke# on a still day. Iron and coal. | My washing comes in greyer than it went out. #annoyed#.
b : It's always the same. | Iron and coal? | Hang it inside.
a : The same, and it never gets cleaner. #annoyed#. | Iron and coal, and something burnt underneath. | Inside it never dries. Outside it never stays clean. Pick one.

scene rain_window
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize#. Nobody on #street# but those who must be. | Wet. #street.capitalize# can do without me in this. | Rain washes #smoke# off the sill. That's the one thing I'll say for it.
b : Stay in, then. | Not for anything? | Something good, then.
a : I'm in. I'm always in. #bc_true#. | Not for bread, not for gossip. It'll keep. | Something. Don't spread it, #address#.

scene good_apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Give me #apple# and a bit of cheese and I want nothing else. | I can tell a good apple from across #street#. The skin tells you. | An apple that bends when you squeeze it isn't worth #copper#.
b : Plain tastes. | Can you? | Fair enough.
a : Plain, and I'll not be talked out of them, #address#. | From across the street. Ask me, if you're buying. | Fair, and true. Hard or nothing.

scene stale_bread
when topic=food|prices self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : The baker passed me #stale# as yesterday's. It was last week's. | #stale.capitalize#. I'll not eat it. I'll feed it to the gulls first. | A crust of fresh over a whole loaf of old, any day. #saying#.
b : Take it back. | The gulls will thank you. | That's fair.
a : I will. And they'll know I've been. | Somebody should. Nobody thanks me. | Fair. And at my time of life my mind stays where it's put.

scene larder_shelf
when topic=home|food self.likes=full_larder
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #larder.capitalize#'s full this week. I keep looking at it. | A full shelf, and winter can howl at the door all it wants. | I've a jar of pickle, a crock of lard and a bag of meal. I count them every night.
b : That's a comfort. | Let it come. | Every night?
a : The only one I need, #address#. | Let it. I'm ready. | Every night, after #jar#. Then I sleep.

scene rats_skirting
when topic=animals|home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : #rats.capitalize# again. I hear them at night, bold as lodgers. | They had the corner off my meal sack. I'll have their tails. | I've put a brick against the hole. #rats.capitalize# made another.
b : Get a cat. | Will you? | They always do.
a : A cat's another mouth. I've enough to feed. | I will. Old I may be, but I'm not slow. | They do. And I always put another brick. #oath#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_true#

scene my_child
when topic=family|friends self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.child# works too hard and eats too little. I've said so, #oath#. | Not where #self.child# can hear, mind, but I'm proud. There. | #self.child# knows to bring me #apple# on Restday. I taught that much.
b : Children never listen. | Say it out loud, then. | You have.
a : Never. I didn't either. #bc_true#. | No. Praise goes to a young head, #address#. | I have. Hard ones, every time.

scene lake_shore_home
when topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : In #self.from_town# there was frost on #shore# like sugar, and you could hear the ice talk. | I left #self.from_town# when I was young and never once went back. I'd not know it now. | At home we'd sit on the jetty in the cold and play cards on an upturned boat.
b[from=coldwater] #cw : The ice talking. I remember. | It's changed, they say. | On a boat! We did too.
b : The ice talks? | Would you go back? | Cards on a boat?
a@cw : Then you know. Nobody here believes me. | Changed, or I have. One or the other. | Then you'll know who always won.
a : Cracks and groans all night. You learn to sleep through it. | No. There's nothing there for me but the cold. | On the bottom of one. It made a fair table, #address#.

scene new_lot
when topic=newcomer|player here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : New lot on the row this week. I've been watching from #window#. | Another family in the end house. They'll be gone by spring. | Every new face makes #street# a bit less ours.
b : Give them a chance. | Will they? | It's a city.
a : I'll give them what I gave the last lot. A look. | They always are. I don't bother learning names now. | A city, aye. That's my complaint, #address#.

scene feast_noise
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Feast nights the racket comes right up to #window#. I shut it and play #cards#. | They'll be singing in #street# till dawn, and somebody'll cry. Every year. | I went to a feast once. I came home with a #stranger#'s ale down my back.
b : It's only once a year. | Somebody always does. | Once was enough?
a : Once is enough, #address#. I'll watch from here. | Every year. Always the same one, too. | Plenty. #oath#.

scene chapel_fed
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : They kept my house fed a lean winter at the chapel. I go when I can, for that alone. | Praying's not my habit. A thank-you, and #copper# goes in the jar. | The Bright One's heard more from me lately. Age does that.
b : That's a good reason. | Thank you's enough. | It does.
a : It's the only reason I need. | I'd hope so. It's all I'll spend. | It does. You've more to say, and less time to say it.

scene gossip_shut
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : Plenty goes past #window#. I keep it behind the glass. | Somebody's been coming and going late on the row. I'll not say who. | I've heard talk. I'm too old to carry it.
b : Go on. | You know who, though. | Not even to me?
a : No. It's theirs, not mine. | I know. That's enough for me, #address#. | Not even to you. #saying#.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene hard_week
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : No #copper# in #jar# last night. First time this year. I didn't like it. | Bread's up again, and not #copper# coming in. I've the parish loaf on the table. | Lean. I've let the fire go out early to save the coal.
b : It'll come back. | No shame in the parish. | Wrap up warm.
a : It will. I'll put two in tomorrow. | None. Pride's for when you've eaten. | I've two shawls. I'll manage. #bc_i_will#.

story the_frozen_lake [topic=memories|season self.away=yes self.from=coldwater self.age>=50]
  : The year I was ten, #shore# froze so hard the carters drove across it to save the long road.
  : #mum.capitalize# wouldn't let me on it. I went anyway, at night, and lay on my back in the middle.
  : The ice groaned under me like an old door. I've never been so frightened or so happy.
  ask : Would you have gone out on that ice?
  b : I'd have been out there beside you.
  b[old] : Never. I'd have stood on the shore and shouted for your mother.

story the_winning_hand [topic=pastimes self.likes=cards self.age>=40]
  : Years back I sat up all night at #cards# with three dockers who thought an old stick was easy coin.
  : By dawn I'd every #copper# they had and one docker's cap.
  : I gave the cap back. The coin went in #jar#. It was the first coin in it.
  b : Ha! That's how it started?
  b[pair.band=friends] : I've heard this one. You still have the cap, don't you.
  : That's how it started. I'll finish it the same way.

story first_copper [topic=dreams|memories self.age>=40]
  : The week I reached the city I swore I'd have a stall of my own by thirty.
  : Thirty came, and forty, and I'd nothing put by but a bad cough.
  : So I started #jar#. One a night. Slow is still going somewhere.
  ask : What would you put by for, if you had a jar?
  b : A dry roof, I think.
  b[wealth=poor|destitute] : I'd need the copper first.

rule @jar_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 12h
say One more in #jar#. There. | #copper.capitalize#. In it goes. #saying#.

rule @rats_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 12h
say I hear you. I'll have you yet. | #rats.capitalize#. #oath#. Not in my meal, you don't.

rule @frost_bark
when concept=bark here.season=winter here.time=dawn here.weather=clear self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #frost.capitalize#. Good. | Look at that glass. #frost.capitalize#.

rule @window_bark
when concept=bark here.time=day here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Late again, that one. Every day this week. | There goes #street#, and not a head turned up at #window#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What do you want? | #greet#. Well, out with it.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You again. Sit, if you're stopping.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. I'm counting into #jar#. Be quick.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say your piece from there. I'm old, not deaf.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.age>=60] : I sit at #window# and watch the world go by. I've earned it. | Nothing, now. I watch #street# and fill #jar#.
dlg @2 resident.job : Whatever I can, and I ask nobody's help with it. | A bit of this, a bit of that. Enough.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Somebody under #window# was saying: word from #world.news_from#, #world.news#. That's all I caught.
dlg @2 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing. #street.capitalize#'s been quiet all week.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I see plenty. I say none of it.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the step. | #farewell#.
graft resident.hub
choice What's in the jar on your shelf? -> jar
node jar
say A copper for every night I've had one spare. When it's full I'll have a market stall of my own, and sell apples, and not haggle with anyone.
mood calm
free
choice How long until it's full? -> jar_long
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node jar_long
say Longer than I've got, maybe. That's no reason to stop. You don't fill a jar by looking at it.
choice I hope you get your stall. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


old
scene old_knees
when topic=health|day
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : My knees argue with every step of the stair these days. | All these winters, and the cold gets in further every one. | I'm tired, that's all. Tired and still here, #address#.
b : Take the rail. | Sit by the fire. | Still here's good.
a : I'll take the rail when I'm dead. Not before. | I'll sit where I like, thank you. | It's something. #bc_mostly#.

scene the_old_days
when topic=memories|times
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : In #olddays# you could walk the roads at night and nobody'd stop you. Not now. | When I was young bread was #copper# and you got change. | I remember when this street had trees. Two, by the pump. Gone for firewood.
b : Things change. | Change from a copper? | Trees, here?
a : Change, aye. Not for the better, mostly. | A half. And they'd give you the heel free. | Two. I watched them come down from #window#. Nobody asked me.

scene pity_refused
when topic=smalltalk|health
does tell.self / disagree / insist / ack
a : Somebody offered to carry my basket today. I told them I'm old, not broken. | A young one from the chapel asked if I wanted help with my stair. I said I wanted help with my rent. | Take that look off your face. Old, aye. Pitied, no.
b : They meant well. | Fair point. | Sorry.
a : They can mean well somewhere else. #saying#. | It was. They didn't laugh. I'd not have minded. | No harm. Only don't do it twice, #address#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_sorry#
